1
00:00:21,479 --> 00:00:26,943
CRIME SCENE ZERO

2
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:31,364
Today, 583 more people
have tested positive for COVID-19.

3
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,867
{\an8}<i>The government has raised the level
of social distancing and banned gatherings</i>

4
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,076
{\an8}<i>of more than five people...</i>

5
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:39,289
{\an8}<i>Tonight, Seoul City is introducing
a citywide shutdown of shops after 9 p.m.,</i>

6
00:00:39,372 --> 00:00:41,249
{\an8}<i>sending a strong message to the public.</i>

7
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:43,251
{\an8}WHOLE CHICKIN

8
00:00:43,334 --> 00:00:44,711
{\an8}<i>Breaking news.</i>

9
00:00:44,794 --> 00:00:48,089
{\an8}<i>Record-breaking heavy rain has caused
severe flooding in the central region...</i>

10
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:52,343
{\an8}<i>Especially in the Gangdam District,
where hourly rainfall of 120 mm</i>

11
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:53,595
{\an8}<i>has caused flooding in many areas...</i>

12
00:00:53,678 --> 00:00:56,681
{\an8}<i>Gangdam District
is working to minimize damage</i>

13
00:00:56,765 --> 00:00:59,684
{\an8}<i>by monitoring precipitation in real time
and closing vulnerable roads.</i>

14
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:01,478
{\an8}GANGDAM DISTRICT
CLOSES ROADS TO MINIMIZE DAMAGE

15
00:01:01,561 --> 00:01:03,063
NO ENTRY
DETOUR ADVISED DUE TO ROAD FLOOD

16
00:01:11,863 --> 00:01:15,784
AUGUST 12, 2020, 12:00 A.M.

17
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:19,329
{\an8}It's the perfect weather
for a crime to occur.

18
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:23,208
Jeez.

19
00:01:24,084 --> 00:01:27,253
What a cruel and chaotic world.

20
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:35,345
{\an8}SELF TEMPERATURE CHECK

21
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:36,304
{\an8}Normal.

22
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:37,847
{\an8}PASSED

23
00:01:39,015 --> 00:01:41,851
{\an8}LEAD INVESTIGATOR ON THE FOURTH CASE
JANG DETECTIVE

24
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:46,397
Oh boy.

25
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:48,691
GANGDAM DISTRICT
TEMPORARY SCREENING CENTER

26
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:51,986
"SOCIAL DISTANCING MEASURES" FOR COVID-19

27
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:57,283
COMBINED WITH UNPRECEDENTED HEAVY RAIN

28
00:01:58,243 --> 00:02:01,204
UNUSUALLY QUIET YOUTH STREET
NEAR GANGDAM STATION

29
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:06,334
THE VICTIM'S LIFELESS BODY
WAS FOUND AT THE HEART OF IT

30
00:02:08,503 --> 00:02:11,756
MURDER IN THE NIGHTLIFE DISTRICT I

31
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:16,761
{\an8}How could a murder like this

32
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:19,848
{\an8}have happened in the heart of Gangdam?

33
00:02:24,227 --> 00:02:25,603
{\an8}How does this make any sense?

34
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:29,691
{\an8}- Hey!
- Detective.

35
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:32,068
{\an8}Hello, sir. AD, reporting for duty.

36
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:32,986
{\an8}Get over here.

37
00:02:33,069 --> 00:02:35,905
{\an8}Who knows what kind of germs
you might be carrying?

38
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:38,408
{\an8}- Okay, you can take off your mask.
- Got it.

39
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:39,325
{\an8}NO GERMS TO TRANSMIT

40
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:40,618
ASSISTANT DETECTIVE
KANG MINHEE

41
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:42,787
Detective, don't tell me you caught it.

42
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:43,705
(THOROUGH)

43
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:47,876
What were you up to
before becoming an assistant detective?

44
00:02:47,959 --> 00:02:49,752
{\an8}I used to dance a little.

45
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:50,879
{\an8}- You danced?
- Yes.

46
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:51,796
{\an8}- Is that so?
- Yes.

47
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,214
{\an8}Show me some moves, then.

48
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:56,551
{\an8}I need to see whether you'll make
a decent assistant detective or not.

49
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:57,802
{\an8}Got it.

50
00:02:59,095 --> 00:03:00,555
{\an8}WARMING UP HIS JOINTS...

51
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:07,228
{\an8}ACK!

52
00:03:09,355 --> 00:03:10,982
{\an8}A RAIN-SOAKED HAZING

53
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:12,650
{\an8}That was part of my performance.

54
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:14,027
{\an8}That was some impressive dancing.

55
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:15,153
{\an8}VERY SATISFIED

56
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:16,613
{\an8}I approve. You pass.

57
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:18,448
{\an8}THE ASSISTANT DETECTIVE
TITLE EARNED THROUGH PAIN

58
00:03:18,531 --> 00:03:21,701
Anyway, what case are we dealing with?
What happened here?

59
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:23,745
To be honest, I had trouble

60
00:03:23,828 --> 00:03:25,580
{\an8}identifying the victim for today's case.

61
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:26,915
{\an8}All I know is
she worked at Sensibility Bar--

62
00:03:26,998 --> 00:03:27,832
{\an8}What?

63
00:03:28,958 --> 00:03:31,044
{\an8}So we don't have anything else
on the victim?

64
00:03:31,127 --> 00:03:32,503
{\an8}At the moment, we don't.

65
00:03:32,587 --> 00:03:34,047
{\an8}Are you kidding me?

66
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:35,965
{\an8}Fine. Do we at least have our suspects?

67
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:38,092
{\an8}Yes, sir. I'll bring them all here.

68
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:40,595
{\an8}- Put the squeeze on them first.
- Yes, sir.

69
00:03:40,678 --> 00:03:43,556
{\an8}They should be taught
who's the boss from the get-go.

70
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:45,141
{\an8}A VICTIM DIFFICULT TO IDENTIFY...

71
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:46,142
{\an8}That weather's awful.

72
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:47,685
{\an8}WHO ARE THE SUSPECTS IN THIS CASE?

73
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:51,231
Any idea why we got called out this late?

74
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:54,108
What's the holdup? Move it along!

75
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:56,236
- Don't you know gatherings are banned?
- Suspects.

76
00:03:56,319 --> 00:03:58,363
Suspects, form a single line.

77
00:03:58,446 --> 00:04:01,241
{\an8}- Keep in mind the times we're in.
- Who are you calling a suspect?

78
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,825
{\an8}Who are you to boss us around?

79
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:06,162
{\an8}I'm the lead detective on this case.

80
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:08,790
{\an8}- A case?
- In light of the pandemic,

81
00:04:08,873 --> 00:04:10,458
{\an8}- I'll check your temperature first.
- Sure.

82
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:11,709
{\an8}THOROUGH TEMPERATURE CHECK

83
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:14,963
{\an8}You're at 36.3°C.

84
00:04:15,046 --> 00:04:16,506
{\an8}- Pass. You may remove your mask.
- Thanks.

85
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:18,466
{\an8}- Wait here.
- What?

86
00:04:18,549 --> 00:04:20,051
{\an8}- Stand by!
- Okay.

87
00:04:20,134 --> 00:04:21,844
{\an8}Repeat the command. Stand by.

88
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:22,804
{\an8}Stand by!

89
00:04:25,014 --> 00:04:26,933
You're at 36.4°C. Pass.

90
00:04:27,767 --> 00:04:30,937
Jeez. What's with all this nonsense?

91
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:33,356
You're at 36.3°C. Pass.

92
00:04:35,566 --> 00:04:36,651
Did you even sanitize this?

93
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:39,237
- Pick up the pace.
- You're at 36.3°C.

94
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,488
- What the...
- What a hassle.

95
00:04:40,571 --> 00:04:41,990
{\an8}Are you serious right now?

96
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:45,410
It's because of the pandemic.

97
00:04:45,493 --> 00:04:48,371
I've been flipping this mask inside out
every three days to get by.

98
00:04:48,454 --> 00:04:49,914
I have no choice but to target your eye.

99
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:50,999
{\an8}A NECESSARY ACTION

100
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:52,500
{\an8}You're at 36.5°C. Pass.

101
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:55,586
{\an8}- But my eyes are intense.
- I'm a busy person, you know.

102
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:58,172
{\an8}- What the heck is going on?
- Why are we here?

103
00:04:58,256 --> 00:04:59,674
{\an8}- All right.
- I've been out all day today.

104
00:04:59,757 --> 00:05:01,426
{\an8}There's been a murder.

105
00:05:01,509 --> 00:05:03,094
{\an8}- What?
- Let's take a look at the crime scene.

106
00:05:03,177 --> 00:05:04,554
{\an8}It's this way. Come with me.

107
00:05:04,637 --> 00:05:08,308
{\an8}- Who in the world died?
- Seems like I'm tangled up in a mess.

108
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:12,979
{\an8}- What is this?
- Who is this?

109
00:05:14,731 --> 00:05:15,565
{\an8}Is that Gun-mi?

110
00:05:16,357 --> 00:05:17,358
{\an8}Gun-mi?

111
00:05:17,442 --> 00:05:18,651
{\an8}- What the heck?
- Is that Gun-mi?

112
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:20,445
{\an8}- Gun-mi?
- It's Lee Gun-mi.

113
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:21,654
{\an8}- Gun-mi!
- Gun-mi?

114
00:05:22,739 --> 00:05:24,615
{\an8}- It's Lee Gun-mi.
- Hold on.

115
00:05:24,699 --> 00:05:25,992
{\an8}Do you know the victim?

116
00:05:26,075 --> 00:05:27,493
{\an8}Gun-mi's my friend.

117
00:05:27,577 --> 00:05:29,412
{\an8}- Gun-mi? What's her last name?
- Yes.

118
00:05:29,495 --> 00:05:30,830
{\an8}- Lee Gun-mi.
- Lee Gun-mi?

119
00:05:30,913 --> 00:05:32,832
{\an8}You know the victim, Ms. Lee Gun-mi?

120
00:05:32,915 --> 00:05:33,958
{\an8}FRIENDS WITH THE VICTIM?

121
00:05:35,251 --> 00:05:36,085
{\an8}Hold on.

122
00:05:37,378 --> 00:05:39,964
{\an8}Since she's your friend,
can I assume she's a woman?

123
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:41,758
{\an8}Anyone can tell she's a woman.

124
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:43,259
{\an8}Let's move things along.

125
00:05:43,801 --> 00:05:46,054
{\an8}You say she's a woman, but...

126
00:05:46,137 --> 00:05:47,597
{\an8}Her neck... Oh jeez!

127
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,514
{\an8}What's wrong?

128
00:05:48,598 --> 00:05:50,058
{\an8}She has an Adam's apple.

129
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:51,809
{\an8}Look.

130
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:52,727
{\an8}What?

131
00:05:53,311 --> 00:05:54,354
What the heck?

132
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:56,814
Detective!

133
00:05:57,690 --> 00:05:59,025
Hey, AD.

134
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:00,360
Here's the victim's file.

135
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:03,279
{\an8}HAS THE VICTIM FINALLY BEEN IDENTIFIED?

136
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:05,406
{\an8}Is that the case? I see.

137
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:10,536
{\an8}The victim is Lee Gun-jun.

138
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:11,496
{\an8}What?

139
00:06:11,579 --> 00:06:14,082
{\an8}A 27-year-old male.

140
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:15,249
{\an8}What?

141
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:17,877
{\an8}Are you saying that's Lee Gun-jun,
not Lee Gun-mi?

142
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:19,629
{\an8}THE VICTIM ISN'T LEE GUN-MI, A WOMAN,
BUT LEE GUN-JUN, A MAN?

143
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:21,381
{\an8}Wait. Gun-jun's my friend.

144
00:06:22,715 --> 00:06:23,800
{\an8}HIS FRIEND?

145
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:25,885
{\an8}Are you saying this is Gun-jun?

146
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:28,679
{\an8}Didn't you hear the detective say
he was 27, you old man?

147
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:29,806
{\an8}How old are you?

148
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:33,226
{\an8}Just so you know, I'm 27.
He's my friend, and we're the same age.

149
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:34,727
{\an8}The world is going mad, isn't it?

150
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,312
{\an8}Come on, Ms. Park. Don't be like that.

151
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:38,815
{\an8}I can tell something's off
about you people already.

152
00:06:39,982 --> 00:06:42,110
<i>The victim is Lee Gun-jun,</i>

153
00:06:42,193 --> 00:06:43,653
<i>a 27-year-old male.</i>

154
00:06:43,736 --> 00:06:44,570
<i>Unemployed.</i>

155
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:46,239
{\an8}<i>His body was discovered</i>

156
00:06:46,322 --> 00:06:48,366
{\an8}<i>in the nightlife district
of Gangdam Station's Youth Street</i>

157
00:06:48,449 --> 00:06:50,743
{\an8}<i>at midnight on the 12th.</i>

158
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:52,829
<i>Exposure to the rain caused inconsistency</i>

159
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:55,206
<i>in the rate
at which the body temperature dropped,</i>

160
00:06:55,289 --> 00:06:58,292
<i>making it impossible
to accurately determine the time of death.</i>

161
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:01,671
The rain not only made it difficult
to estimate the time of death

162
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:04,048
but also wiped away the victim's blood

163
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:06,050
and potential evidence
left behind by the culprit.

164
00:07:06,134 --> 00:07:08,761
This puts us in a very tough spot.

165
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:11,639
{\an8}Business was already bad around here,
and now this?

166
00:07:11,722 --> 00:07:13,141
{\an8}Bad luck just doesn't let up, does it?

167
00:07:13,724 --> 00:07:16,894
{\an8}- Let's catch who did it.
- Form a single line and follow me.

168
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:19,772
{\an8}Don't you dare slip away and come with me.

169
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:21,524
{\an8}I need to get back to the store.

170
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:23,568
DIGGING INTO THE SUSPECTS

171
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:24,819
We're in for a ride today.

172
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:26,946
<i>First suspect, Kim Club.</i>

173
00:07:27,029 --> 00:07:28,614
<i>A 57-year-old male.</i>

174
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:30,783
<i>Owner of Club Slam.</i>

175
00:07:30,867 --> 00:07:32,785
<i>Second suspect, An Dancer.</i>

176
00:07:32,869 --> 00:07:34,245
<i>A 27-year-old female.</i>

177
00:07:34,328 --> 00:07:36,456
<i>Dancer at Club Slam.</i>

178
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:38,624
<i>Third suspect, Park Chicken.</i>

179
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:40,126
<i>A 38-year-old female.</i>

180
00:07:40,209 --> 00:07:42,044
<i>Owner of a fried chicken restaurant.</i>

181
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:44,213
<i>Fourth suspect, Jang C-store.</i>

182
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:45,715
<i>A 27-year-old male.</i>

183
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:47,758
<i>Part-timer at a convenience store.</i>

184
00:07:47,842 --> 00:07:49,969
<i>Fifth suspect, Ha Gold Spoon.</i>

185
00:07:50,052 --> 00:07:51,429
<i>A 32-year-old male.</i>

186
00:07:51,512 --> 00:07:56,100
<i>Attorney and mediator
of the Gangdam District lease dispute.</i>

187
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:58,811
Let's hurry up and catch the culprit

188
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:02,356
so the victim's soul can find peace
after the wrongful death.

189
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:04,066
- Got it?
- Who knows if it was wrongful?

190
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:06,611
All right. Let's begin the investigation.

191
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:09,697
{\an8}The first thing we need to clarify

192
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:13,993
{\an8}is whether you knew the victim
as Lee Gun-mi or Lee Gun-jun.

193
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:15,411
{\an8}That's crucial.

194
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:16,954
{\an8}- Mr. Kim Club.
- Yes?

195
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:21,250
{\an8}Please introduce yourself
and how you knew the victim.

196
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:22,502
{\an8}Sure thing.

197
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:26,714
{\an8}I'm the owner of the hottest club
near Gangdam Station in Gangdam District.

198
00:08:26,797 --> 00:08:28,174
{\an8}- It's called Club Slam.
-"Club Slam"?

199
00:08:28,257 --> 00:08:31,177
{\an8}- I run a club near Gangdam Station.
- Okay.

200
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:32,637
{\an8}The victim, did you say?

201
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:33,554
{\an8}Yes.

202
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:34,722
{\an8}Lee Gun-mi, was it?

203
00:08:34,805 --> 00:08:38,434
{\an8}The victim's name was Lee Gun-jun,
not Lee Gun-mi.

204
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:41,103
{\an8}That darn brat was a guy.

205
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:42,939
{\an8}Are you saying
you didn't know he was a man?

206
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:45,233
{\an8}I thought he was a she.

207
00:08:45,316 --> 00:08:48,194
{\an8}So you had no idea
that the victim was a man?

208
00:08:48,277 --> 00:08:50,154
How would I have known that?

209
00:08:50,238 --> 00:08:51,239
Understood.

210
00:08:51,322 --> 00:08:53,324
We'll move on to Ms. Park Chicken.

211
00:08:53,407 --> 00:08:56,786
{\an8}Right. Well, I've been running
a fried chicken restaurant

212
00:08:56,869 --> 00:08:58,204
{\an8}for just over a year now.

213
00:08:58,287 --> 00:08:59,247
{\an8}- A year?
- That's right.

214
00:08:59,330 --> 00:09:01,541
{\an8}I knew the victim as Lee Gun-mi,

215
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:05,169
{\an8}and we've been friends for several years.

216
00:09:05,253 --> 00:09:09,507
{\an8}So you and Ms. Lee Gun-mi were friends?

217
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:12,843
We used to keep in touch regularly,

218
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:15,304
but then drifted apart.

219
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:17,807
- We only recently reconnected.
- Hold on.

220
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:19,517
Ms. Park is one scary woman.

221
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:22,270
Wait. Are those tattoos on your arms?

222
00:09:22,353 --> 00:09:24,230
{\an8}Yes. Is having tattoos against the law?

223
00:09:24,313 --> 00:09:26,732
{\an8}Do you slaughter the chickens yourself?

224
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:28,734
{\an8}Why is your apron covered in blood?

225
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:32,738
{\an8}I'm all about serving fried chicken
from freshly butchered chickens.

226
00:09:32,822 --> 00:09:35,366
My restaurant is pretty well-known
around Gangdam District.

227
00:09:35,449 --> 00:09:37,702
Do you always wear your hair like that
while frying chicken?

228
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:39,620
- Got a problem with it?
- Are those horns or what?

229
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:41,414
{\an8}My customers say
they look like drumsticks,

230
00:09:41,497 --> 00:09:42,623
{\an8}but it's actually for hygiene.

231
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:45,251
{\an8}The fried chicken lady
with the drumstick hairstyle.

232
00:09:45,334 --> 00:09:46,794
{\an8}Let's move on to Mr. Ha Gold Spoon.

233
00:09:46,877 --> 00:09:48,629
{\an8}- Sure thing.
- Please go ahead.

234
00:09:49,213 --> 00:09:51,424
Honestly, I don't even know why I'm here.

235
00:09:51,507 --> 00:09:53,801
- I save lives, not take them away.
- He's hot.

236
00:09:53,884 --> 00:09:55,011
- Isn't he super hot?
- Is that so?

237
00:09:55,094 --> 00:09:57,972
I'm working as the mediator
of the Gangdam District

238
00:09:58,055 --> 00:09:59,599
{\an8}commercial property lease dispute.

239
00:10:00,516 --> 00:10:03,311
{\an8}However, my main job is an attorney.

240
00:10:03,394 --> 00:10:04,729
{\an8}My family members

241
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:07,148
have practiced law for generations,

242
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:09,483
so I naturally chose the same path.

243
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:12,153
Hey, Detective. Let's send this guy home.

244
00:10:12,236 --> 00:10:13,571
- Yes, let's.
- He couldn't have done this.

245
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:15,031
That's for me to decide!

246
00:10:15,114 --> 00:10:17,158
{\an8}Gold Spoon's not the type
to be in this part of town.

247
00:10:17,241 --> 00:10:20,286
{\an8}- He's on the suspect list.
- Did you call him by name?

248
00:10:20,369 --> 00:10:22,705
{\an8}Did I hear that right?
Are you on a first-name basis?

249
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:24,165
{\an8}- Look here.
- Mr. Gold Spoon.

250
00:10:24,248 --> 00:10:25,625
{\an8}Is that how things are?

251
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:29,003
{\an8}I serve the public, so why am I here
being treated like a criminal?

252
00:10:29,086 --> 00:10:31,297
{\an8}- I can vouch for this man.
- Right.

253
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:32,798
{\an8}He's actually my landlord.

254
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:35,468
{\an8}- Everyone around here knows him.
- In Gangdam District...

255
00:10:35,551 --> 00:10:37,845
{\an8}Are you a landlord?

256
00:10:37,928 --> 00:10:41,515
{\an8}I sure am. Goldspoon Buildings 1 and 2
are registered in my name.

257
00:10:41,599 --> 00:10:42,850
{\an8}I see, sir.

258
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:44,602
{\an8}(SUDDENLY SHOWING RESPECT)

259
00:10:45,186 --> 00:10:46,854
{\an8}I'll do my best
to make you comfortable today.

260
00:10:46,937 --> 00:10:48,022
{\an8}Do you need an office?

261
00:10:48,564 --> 00:10:49,440
Well, kind of.

262
00:10:49,523 --> 00:10:51,942
- I'll let you know if a spot opens up.
- Sure.

263
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:52,860
Anyway,

264
00:10:52,943 --> 00:10:55,529
did you know the victim,

265
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:59,158
either as Lee Gun-jun or Lee Gun-mi?

266
00:10:59,241 --> 00:11:02,370
I went to Sensibility Bar to grab a drink
by myself and met the victim,

267
00:11:02,453 --> 00:11:03,996
who was working part-time.

268
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:06,415
{\an8}- That's when we got to know each other.
- Sensibility Bar?

269
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:10,419
{\an8}Was the victim working part-time
as Lee Gun-jun or Lee Gun-mi?

270
00:11:10,503 --> 00:11:12,254
{\an8}She was working there as Lee Gun-mi.

271
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:13,964
{\an8}Lee Gun-mi worked part-time.

272
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:15,549
{\an8}- And that's how you met her?
- That's right.

273
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:16,926
I'm shocked

274
00:11:17,009 --> 00:11:19,178
by what Ms. Chicken, Mr. Club,

275
00:11:19,261 --> 00:11:21,972
{\an8}- and Mr. Attorney just said.
- Why's that?

276
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:25,559
{\an8}Because that's definitely Gun-jun,
my classmate from high school.

277
00:11:25,643 --> 00:11:26,477
{\an8}- What?
- Yeah.

278
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,645
{\an8}What are you on about?

279
00:11:27,728 --> 00:11:30,231
{\an8}I can't believe
he's been living as a woman,

280
00:11:30,314 --> 00:11:33,442
{\an8}partying and working part-time.

281
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:36,529
{\an8}I'm just so shocked
by everything I've just heard.

282
00:11:36,612 --> 00:11:38,447
{\an8}I had absolutely no idea.

283
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:41,826
{\an8}Anyway, I work part-time
at a local convenience store.

284
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:44,537
{\an8}My name's Jang C-store.

285
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:46,247
You might know this already,

286
00:11:46,330 --> 00:11:48,582
but I work longer hours
than most part-timers.

287
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:51,293
I see him at the store whenever I drop by.

288
00:11:51,377 --> 00:11:52,461
{\an8}- He's very hardworking.
- Very.

289
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:55,464
{\an8}Morning, evening, or night.
He's always there.

290
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:57,758
{\an8}Judging by his looks,
I thought he was the owner.

291
00:11:57,842 --> 00:11:59,093
Just to avoid any misunderstandings,

292
00:11:59,176 --> 00:12:00,928
I really am 27.

293
00:12:01,011 --> 00:12:03,556
- You seem like a nice guy.
- We're the same age.

294
00:12:03,639 --> 00:12:06,058
Keep reminding us
so we won't get confused.

295
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:07,893
- We're the same age.
- This is a crazy world.

296
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:09,645
You must find it easy
to speak casually to him, then.

297
00:12:09,729 --> 00:12:12,565
Why would I be uncomfortable
when we're the same age, Gold Spoon?

298
00:12:12,648 --> 00:12:14,692
Since you're talking,
we'll move on to you, Ms. An Dancer.

299
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:18,696
Okay. I'm An Dancer, Gun-mi's best friend.

300
00:12:18,779 --> 00:12:20,281
Mr. Kim Club is my boss.

301
00:12:20,364 --> 00:12:22,283
{\an8}I work as a dancer at his club.

302
00:12:22,366 --> 00:12:24,410
{\an8}- She's one of my employees.
- At Club Slam?

303
00:12:24,493 --> 00:12:29,039
{\an8}You said you were friends
with the victim, Ms. Lee Gun-mi.

304
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:31,041
{\an8}Yes, we were best friends.

305
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:35,087
{\an8}To be honest, I knew.

306
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:36,046
{\an8}Knew what?

307
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:38,924
{\an8}I knew she was actually a guy.

308
00:12:39,008 --> 00:12:40,634
{\an8}- What?
- You knew?

309
00:12:40,718 --> 00:12:44,680
{\an8}You became best friends with Lee Gun-mi
despite knowing she was actually a guy?

310
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:46,348
{\an8}We were best friends from the beginning.

311
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:50,019
{\an8}We were close enough
that we eventually shared our secrets.

312
00:12:50,102 --> 00:12:51,228
{\an8}She told me herself.

313
00:12:51,312 --> 00:12:56,567
{\an8}Did the victim want to transition
to become a woman?

314
00:12:56,650 --> 00:12:58,527
{\an8}Yes, she was a woman at heart.

315
00:12:58,611 --> 00:12:59,779
{\an8}A woman at heart, huh?
Yes.

316
00:13:00,654 --> 00:13:03,783
{\an8}We couldn't get an accurate read
on the victim's body temperature

317
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:07,119
{\an8}due to exposure to the heavy rain.

318
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:10,664
{\an8}And that means, we can't pin down
the estimated time of death.

319
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:11,874
{\an8}Oh dear.

320
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:15,503
{\an8}I'd like to know the last time
each of you saw the victim,

321
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:18,380
{\an8}either as Lee Gun-jun or Lee Gun-mi.

322
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:19,673
{\an8}I didn't see him.

323
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:22,593
{\an8}Were you working
at the convenience store yesterday?

324
00:13:22,676 --> 00:13:24,512
{\an8}- I was.
- You were on shift,

325
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:27,056
{\an8}but you didn't notice anything going on
in the empty lot next to the store?

326
00:13:27,139 --> 00:13:31,101
{\an8}No, and just so you know,
Gun-jun lived above the convenience store.

327
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:33,187
{\an8}- Yet, you didn't see him?
- No, I didn't see him yesterday.

328
00:13:33,270 --> 00:13:34,897
{\an8}- Are you sure?
- He could be lying.

329
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,023
{\an8}That's rather suspicious.

330
00:13:36,106 --> 00:13:37,149
{\an8}What about you, Mr. Club?

331
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:40,319
{\an8}I saw her around 8:20 p.m.

332
00:13:40,402 --> 00:13:42,279
{\an8}- Did you say 8:20 p.m.?
- It was around then. Yes.

333
00:13:42,363 --> 00:13:43,197
{\an8}Where did you see her?

334
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:45,491
{\an8}In front of her place.

335
00:13:45,574 --> 00:13:47,701
{\an8}I see. So, you saw her.

336
00:13:47,785 --> 00:13:49,078
{\an8}What about you, ma'am?

337
00:13:49,161 --> 00:13:52,581
{\an8}I think it was a little over 9 p.m.

338
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,583
{\an8}- I saw her outside her place.
- Outside her home?

339
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:56,418
{\an8}You saw her outside her home.

340
00:13:56,502 --> 00:13:57,336
{\an8}What?

341
00:13:57,419 --> 00:14:00,965
{\an8}Ms. Chicken's account
just jogged my memory.

342
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:05,302
{\an8}I saw them arguing at around 9:15 p.m.

343
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:07,513
{\an8}We didn't meet up or anything.
I just happened to see it.

344
00:14:07,596 --> 00:14:08,722
{\an8}I'll take your word for now.

345
00:14:08,806 --> 00:14:11,016
{\an8}The truth will come out
once we investigate.

346
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:13,269
{\an8}- That sounds suspicious.
- You'll be in big trouble if you lie.

347
00:14:13,352 --> 00:14:15,312
{\an8}What about you, sir?

348
00:14:15,396 --> 00:14:18,482
{\an8}I bumped into her briefly yesterday.

349
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:20,860
{\an8}Around what time and where?

350
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:22,945
{\an8}It was past 9 p.m...

351
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:24,113
{\an8}Let me think.

352
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:25,865
{\an8}It was around 9:45 p.m.

353
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:27,700
{\an8}- Around 9:45?
- Around 9:45?

354
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:30,119
{\an8}- Where?
- Right here. Outside my office.

355
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:32,371
{\an8}Outside your office?
She didn't come inside?

356
00:14:32,454 --> 00:14:33,539
{\an8}No, she didn't.

357
00:14:33,622 --> 00:14:36,584
{\an8}You ran into her outside your office.
How did she seem?

358
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:39,587
{\an8}I can't recall the details,

359
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:42,131
{\an8}but she seemed to be in a hurry.

360
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:43,507
{\an8}In a hurry?

361
00:14:44,508 --> 00:14:46,927
{\an8}<i>Ha Gold Spoon said he saw her at 9:45 p.m.</i>

362
00:14:47,011 --> 00:14:49,930
{\an8}<i>Isn't the last person
to see the victim alive</i>

363
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:51,307
{\an8}<i>usually the most suspicious?</i>

364
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:53,684
{\an8}<i>No one saw her after that
because she was dead by then.</i>

365
00:14:53,767 --> 00:14:58,439
{\an8}Assuming you're all telling the truth,

366
00:14:58,522 --> 00:15:00,149
{\an8}the estimated time of death

367
00:15:00,232 --> 00:15:06,155
{\an8}is between 9:45 p.m. and midnight.

368
00:15:06,238 --> 00:15:08,699
{\an8}Now, please tell me
what you were doing during that time.

369
00:15:08,782 --> 00:15:10,576
{\an8}I'd appreciate full honesty.

370
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:12,661
I probably look
the most suspicious right now,

371
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:14,747
so I'll tell you
how my evening went first.

372
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:18,959
I was in a meeting with business owners
who were affected by COVID-19.

373
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:20,794
- A meeting?
- Yes, it was held right here.

374
00:15:20,878 --> 00:15:22,880
- He's telling the truth.
- You can see the banner over there.

375
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,634
"Gangdam Station Youth Street Meeting

376
00:15:26,717 --> 00:15:29,303
With Business Owners
Affected by COVID-19."

377
00:15:29,386 --> 00:15:31,305
- You hosted that meeting?
- I did.

378
00:15:31,388 --> 00:15:35,726
{\an8}I personally secured the support fund
from the Gangdam District Head.

379
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:38,687
{\an8}Hoping to be of some help
to business owners,

380
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:41,482
{\an8}I used my gift of persuasion
on the District Head.

381
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:43,817
{\an8}Okay, when did the meeting end?

382
00:15:43,901 --> 00:15:47,571
{\an8}I gave legal advice until midnight,
so my alibi is solid.

383
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:49,490
{\an8}- So, you were in a meeting.
- That's right.

384
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:50,741
{\an8}And you, Mr. Club?

385
00:15:50,824 --> 00:15:52,493
{\an8}I was here with my landlord.

386
00:15:52,576 --> 00:15:54,745
{\an8}After all,
I'm also a small local business owner.

387
00:15:54,828 --> 00:15:59,375
{\an8}- You attended the meeting?
- Yes, I arrived at around 9:30 p.m.

388
00:15:59,458 --> 00:16:01,669
{\an8}- Did you sign the document?
- Of course.

389
00:16:01,752 --> 00:16:04,838
{\an8}- And Ms. Dancer?
- I also went to the meeting

390
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:07,049
{\an8}on behalf of the owner of Sensibility Bar.

391
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:08,676
{\an8}Was the whole neighborhood there or what?

392
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:09,927
{\an8}You had to attend to receive aid.

393
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:11,011
{\an8}NO SUPPORT FUND FOR ABSENTEES

394
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:12,429
{\an8}Dancer's one of my employees,

395
00:16:12,513 --> 00:16:14,682
{\an8}but something came up
for the owner of Sensibility Bar,

396
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:17,685
{\an8}so I brought her along to the meeting

397
00:16:17,768 --> 00:16:19,436
{\an8}so she could represent them.

398
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,980
{\an8}Understood.

399
00:16:21,063 --> 00:16:22,189
{\an8}What about you, kid?

400
00:16:24,566 --> 00:16:26,485
{\an8}Can you also call me by my name,
Detective?

401
00:16:26,568 --> 00:16:29,363
{\an8}- I want to be called by my name.
- Do you?

402
00:16:29,446 --> 00:16:31,281
{\an8}The more I see him,
the younger he appears.

403
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:32,616
{\an8}- C-store.
- Yes?

404
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:33,993
{\an8}What were you up to?

405
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:35,494
{\an8}I was also at the meeting.

406
00:16:35,577 --> 00:16:36,745
{\an8}- You were at the meeting too?
- Yes.

407
00:16:36,829 --> 00:16:38,539
{\an8}- I also--
- What about your shift?

408
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:41,041
{\an8}I got here after my shift, so I was late.

409
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:45,045
{\an8}In that case, Ms. Chicken,
you must've been at the meeting too.

410
00:16:45,129 --> 00:16:47,756
{\an8}- I didn't even bother registering.
- What?

411
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,216
{\an8}My life's kept me on my toes.

412
00:16:49,299 --> 00:16:52,803
{\an8}You were on your toes?
Isn't that all the more reason to attend?

413
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:54,471
{\an8}- Anyway, you didn't attend?
- No.

414
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:57,349
{\an8}I wasn't desperate for money,
so I didn't bother registering.

415
00:16:57,433 --> 00:16:59,059
{\an8}Instead, I handled other matters.

416
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:00,477
{\an8}Understood.

417
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:05,232
{\an8}So, while the four of them
were in the same place,

418
00:17:05,315 --> 00:17:07,860
{\an8}you were handling personal matters.

419
00:17:08,736 --> 00:17:10,612
{\an8}Anyway, starting now,

420
00:17:10,696 --> 00:17:13,532
{\an8}you will assist me
in identifying the culprit.

421
00:17:13,615 --> 00:17:17,453
{\an8}You will investigate the scene
in teams of two.

422
00:17:17,536 --> 00:17:19,538
{\an8}- To prove your innocence,
- What a nuisance.

423
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:21,790
{\an8}you must catch the culprit. Got it?

424
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:24,960
{\an8}I will find out who did this
to avenge my friend.

425
00:17:25,044 --> 00:17:27,212
{\an8}How will we be paired up?

426
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:28,797
{\an8}You want me to pair you
with your friend?

427
00:17:29,715 --> 00:17:31,508
{\an8}(NO, WITH GOLD SPOON♥)

428
00:17:31,592 --> 00:17:33,135
{\an8}You've got to be kidding me.

429
00:17:33,218 --> 00:17:36,555
{\an8}I'll give you what you want.

430
00:17:36,638 --> 00:17:37,639
{\an8}Take your friend with you.

431
00:17:38,432 --> 00:17:40,559
{\an8}- Let's do our best with the investigation.
- Sure.

432
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:41,477
{\an8}Shall we?

433
00:17:42,644 --> 00:17:43,729
I can't believe what happened.

434
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:46,023
The business owners
are worried sick as it is.

435
00:17:46,106 --> 00:17:47,024
EXAMINING THE SCENE

436
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:49,234
{\an8}THE NIGHT OF AUGUST 12, 2020

437
00:17:49,818 --> 00:17:51,904
{\an8}SOCIAL DISTANCING

438
00:17:51,987 --> 00:17:53,405
{\an8}AND HEAVY RAIN

439
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:56,909
{\an8}GANGDAM STATION'S YOUTH STREET
WAS ALL BUT EMPTY

440
00:17:58,243 --> 00:18:00,370
{\an8}MEANWHILE

441
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:02,206
{\an8}IN AN EMPTY LOT

442
00:18:02,915 --> 00:18:05,334
{\an8}THE VICTIM WAS FOUND DEAD

443
00:18:07,961 --> 00:18:09,630
EMPTY LOT, LEE GUN-JUN'S HOUSE

444
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:12,091
{\an8}JANG C-STORE'S CONVENIENCE STORE,
GANGDAM POLICE AGENCY, HANSIM POCHA

445
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:13,759
{\an8}GANGSTER WHOLE CHICKEN, CLUB SLAM

446
00:18:13,842 --> 00:18:16,553
{\an8}HA GOLD SPOON'S OFFICE, SENSIBILITY BAR

447
00:18:17,137 --> 00:18:20,849
{\an8}INITIAL EXAMINATION OF CRIME SCENE
COLLECT CLUES FOR 15 MINUTES IN PAIRS

448
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:22,601
- C-store.
- Yeah?

449
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:25,562
{\an8}You botched my shot
at getting paired up with Gold Spoon.

450
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:29,191
{\an8}I'm struggling enough as it is,
and now a person's dead.

451
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:32,319
{\an8}We'll have even fewer people
in the streets at night now.

452
00:18:32,402 --> 00:18:33,654
{\an8}Tonight's the night.

453
00:18:34,738 --> 00:18:36,073
{\an8}I'll look into every angle.

454
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:37,866
{\an8}TEAM 3: JANG DETECTIVE & PARK CHICKEN

455
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:39,576
So, Gun-mi was a man, huh?

456
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:41,912
