457
00:18:43,247 --> 00:18:45,541
{\an8}AN EMPTY LOT IN THE CORNER
OF GANGDAM STATION'S YOUTH STREET

458
00:18:45,624 --> 00:18:46,792
GANGDAM DISTRICT
TEMPORARY SCREENING CENTER

459
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:49,920
{\an8}A TEMPORARY COVID-19 SCREENING CENTER
IS SET UP IN ONE CORNER

460
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,924
{\an8}CONSTRUCTION MATERIALS
ARE SCATTERED EVERYWHERE

461
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:57,302
{\an8}<i>The body was found in an empty lot.</i>

462
00:18:57,386 --> 00:19:00,556
{\an8}<i>Due to the rain,
the bloodstains and other evidence</i>

463
00:19:00,639 --> 00:19:03,725
{\an8}<i>had already been washed away.</i>

464
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:08,438
{\an8}<i>It's possible that the culprit's traces
were washed away as well.</i>

465
00:19:08,522 --> 00:19:10,983
{\an8}I don't think this case
will be an easy one to solve.

466
00:19:11,650 --> 00:19:14,027
{\an8}That little...

467
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:15,821
{\an8}Oh no, my poor Gun-mi.

468
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:17,322
{\an8}Man, what a shame, Gun-jun.

469
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:19,908
{\an8}Gun-jun, was it?

470
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:21,994
{\an8}The kid had me completely fooled.

471
00:19:22,703 --> 00:19:24,997
{\an8}I thought she was a woman.
How was I supposed to know otherwise?

472
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:26,957
{\an8}Is that why she always wore a scarf?

473
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:28,834
{\an8}That explains the scarf.

474
00:19:28,917 --> 00:19:31,545
{\an8}- Detective, doesn't her neck look chafed?
- Hold on.

475
00:19:31,628 --> 00:19:33,213
{\an8}Isn't that a strangulation mark?

476
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:34,840
{\an8}You're right. There's some redness.

477
00:19:34,923 --> 00:19:37,176
{\an8}Considering the mark,
she was likely strangled to death.

478
00:19:37,259 --> 00:19:38,218
{\an8}Look at her head.

479
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:42,139
{\an8}She has a deep gash on her head.

480
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:43,932
{\an8}- You're right.
- That's pretty deep.

481
00:19:44,016 --> 00:19:47,269
{\an8}It looks like it was made
with a claw hammer.

482
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:50,105
{\an8}What's this?

483
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:53,108
{\an8}What happened here?
Did something chafe her back?

484
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:55,152
{\an8}Doesn't it look like
something was scraped against it?

485
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:57,404
{\an8}Are these scratches from fingernails?
What are these marks?

486
00:19:58,030 --> 00:20:00,991
{\an8}She also has wounds
on the back of her hands.

487
00:20:01,074 --> 00:20:03,285
{\an8}It clearly got physical.

488
00:20:03,368 --> 00:20:05,954
{\an8}It's safe to say she was in a fistfight.

489
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:07,414
{\an8}- She's pretty banged up.
- Exactly.

490
00:20:08,665 --> 00:20:11,001
{\an8}What could've been the murder weapon?

491
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:13,587
{\an8}Was she attacked with a shovel?

492
00:20:18,091 --> 00:20:18,967
{\an8}This shovel...

493
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:23,222
DID HE FIND THE MURDER WEAPON?

494
00:20:24,139 --> 00:20:25,641
Goodness. What do we have here?

495
00:20:26,433 --> 00:20:28,185
- Hey, C-store.
- Yeah?

496
00:20:28,268 --> 00:20:30,062
Aren't her shoes too clean?

497
00:20:30,145 --> 00:20:31,563
{\an8}It could be because of the rain.

498
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:34,274
{\an8}- Were the soles washed clean?
- It could've washed the soles clean.

499
00:20:36,818 --> 00:20:38,320
{\an8}Let's check her purse.

500
00:20:38,403 --> 00:20:39,780
{\an8}EXAMINING THE VICTIM'S BELONGINGS

501
00:20:39,863 --> 00:20:41,365
{\an8}There's quite a bit of stuff here.

502
00:20:41,448 --> 00:20:42,908
{\an8}Jeez, this is a lot.

503
00:20:43,617 --> 00:20:44,826
{\an8}A passport? Was he going somewhere?

504
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:47,496
{\an8}Why else would he have a passport on him?

505
00:20:47,579 --> 00:20:48,830
{\an8}Why was she carrying around a passport

506
00:20:48,914 --> 00:20:51,458
{\an8}when she's never even
traveled abroad before?

507
00:20:51,541 --> 00:20:53,418
{\an8}She's been making a lot of money.

508
00:20:53,502 --> 00:20:57,130
"Kim Sucker, Lightweight,
Richie, Han Sucker."

509
00:20:57,214 --> 00:20:59,508
She got a lot of money
out of these suckers.

510
00:20:59,591 --> 00:21:02,803
She also got her deposit back,
so she must've been planning to move out.

511
00:21:02,886 --> 00:21:04,638
{\an8}I guess she was planning to
leave the country.

512
00:21:04,721 --> 00:21:07,307
{\an8}- Probably to run away abroad or something.
- What's this?

513
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:10,435
{\an8}FUNGMU AIR, E-TICKET

514
00:21:10,519 --> 00:21:11,979
{\an8}She booked a flight to Russia.

515
00:21:12,062 --> 00:21:13,063
{\an8}Russia?

516
00:21:13,146 --> 00:21:15,065
{\an8}She was going to take the redeye tonight,

517
00:21:15,148 --> 00:21:17,359
{\an8}but missed the 11:59 p.m. flight.

518
00:21:21,446 --> 00:21:22,406
{\an8}LEE GUN-JUN'S PHONE

519
00:21:22,489 --> 00:21:23,699
{\an8}What is it?

520
00:21:23,782 --> 00:21:25,826
{\an8}- She had been texting.
- About what?

521
00:21:25,909 --> 00:21:28,245
{\an8}It was with Jang C-store,
the convenience store part-timer.

522
00:21:28,328 --> 00:21:30,539
{\an8}C-store, you little punk!

523
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:31,623
{\an8}What are the texts about?

524
00:21:31,707 --> 00:21:32,541
MESSAGES

525
00:21:32,624 --> 00:21:34,459
She wrote, "Hope you're ready."

526
00:21:34,543 --> 00:21:35,502
"Hope you're ready"?

527
00:21:37,963 --> 00:21:39,673
C-store called her at 9:57 p.m.

528
00:21:39,756 --> 00:21:42,467
{\an8}What the hell? C-store, you little...

529
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:47,806
{\an8}Mr. Attorney, I see you've exchanged
messages with Gun-jun.

530
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,433
{\an8}MESSAGES WITH HA GOLD SPOON

531
00:21:49,516 --> 00:21:50,851
{\an8}"How about a drink?"

532
00:21:50,934 --> 00:21:51,977
{\an8}"I'm in. When?"

533
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:53,312
{\an8}"How's today?"

534
00:21:53,395 --> 00:21:55,731
{\an8}"Meet me at my usual lounge bar."

535
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:57,399
{\an8}Who says we can't be friends?

536
00:21:57,482 --> 00:22:01,236
{\an8}- And here I thought you were a decent guy.
- There's nothing to it.

537
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,446
{\an8}Besides, we didn't meet up.

538
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:04,072
{\an8}You didn't?

539
00:22:05,490 --> 00:22:07,451
{\an8}THE VICTIM'S WALLET

540
00:22:07,534 --> 00:22:08,744
ID CARD

541
00:22:08,827 --> 00:22:09,995
She had a fake ID for Lee Gun-mi.

542
00:22:10,078 --> 00:22:11,747
OFFICIAL ID: LEE GUN-JUN
FAKE ID: LEE GUN-MI

543
00:22:13,623 --> 00:22:16,001
Gold Spoon's one generous man.

544
00:22:16,084 --> 00:22:19,463
{\an8}This 50-million-won check
was issued by Ha Gold Spoon.

545
00:22:20,130 --> 00:22:21,465
{\an8}Mr. Attorney.

546
00:22:21,548 --> 00:22:23,008
{\an8}- Yes?
- This is awfully suspicious.

547
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:25,927
{\an8}Well...

548
00:22:26,011 --> 00:22:28,347
{\an8}- I knew her as Gun-mi.
- Smile.

549
00:22:30,307 --> 00:22:31,558
{\an8}MR. SUSPICIOUS ATTORNEY

550
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:32,934
{\an8}That's a great shot.

551
00:22:33,769 --> 00:22:36,438
Goldspoon Buildings 1 and 2.

552
00:22:37,481 --> 00:22:40,859
Why did a guy who owns two buildings
do such a thing?

553
00:22:41,693 --> 00:22:44,237
HA GOLD SPOON'S OFFICE

554
00:22:44,321 --> 00:22:46,031
{\an8}LET US HELP WITH THE LEASE DISPUTE
CAUSED BY COVID-19!

555
00:22:46,114 --> 00:22:47,366
{\an8}GANGDAM DISTRICT
LEASE DISPUTE CONSULTATION CENTER

556
00:22:47,949 --> 00:22:50,452
{\an8}OPERATING AS A CONSULTATION CENTER
FOR THE GANGDAM DISTRICT LEASE DISPUTES

557
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:53,830
{\an8}HA GOLD SPOON'S OFFICE

558
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:57,334
{\an8}"Department of Business Administration."

559
00:22:57,417 --> 00:23:00,670
{\an8}"Master's Program at the School of Law."

560
00:23:00,754 --> 00:23:03,590
{\an8}"Illyu University School of Law
Graduation Ceremony."

561
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:04,716
{\an8}Is that his father?

