00:23:08,887 --> 00:23:09,763
{\an8}What's this?

564
00:23:11,431 --> 00:23:13,308
{\an8}Gucci and Louis Vuitton.

565
00:23:13,392 --> 00:23:15,102
{\an8}LUXURY ITEMS RECEIVED AS GIFTS?

566
00:23:18,230 --> 00:23:21,400
{\an8}"The support fund will be a big help
when you run for the National Assembly."

567
00:23:21,483 --> 00:23:23,860
{\an8}"Remember who got you this far,
and don't screw up."

568
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:25,987
{\an8}"Stay focused, and don't screw up."

569
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:28,031
{\an8}What's all this about not screwing up?

570
00:23:28,115 --> 00:23:29,408
{\an8}"Don't screw up."

571
00:23:29,491 --> 00:23:31,410
{\an8}"Don't embarrass your father..."
These must be from his father.

572
00:23:31,493 --> 00:23:33,745
{\an8}A JOURNALIST AT SPRINT NEWS
WILL PUBLISH AN ARTICLE, SO DON'T SCREW UP

573
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:35,539
<i>Sprint News</i>, huh?

574
00:23:37,249 --> 00:23:39,584
"A Meeting With Business Owners
Impacted by COVID-19 Is Underway."

575
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:42,712
"After Ha Mediator became aware
of the business owners' difficulties..."

576
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:45,215
How did Gold Spoon
come up with such a good idea?

577
00:23:50,053 --> 00:23:52,180
{\an8}This guy's not so clean, is he?

578
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:53,140
{\an8}BUSINESS CARDS FROM FANCY BARS

579
00:23:53,223 --> 00:23:55,475
{\an8}He goes to the bar run by Xi Manager,

580
00:23:55,559 --> 00:23:57,477
{\an8}the one run by Jeong Tender,

581
00:23:57,561 --> 00:23:59,855
{\an8}and even the one run by Kim Piano Key.

582
00:24:00,564 --> 00:24:02,190
{\an8}No wonder I liked him.

583
00:24:03,817 --> 00:24:05,277
{\an8}"Sensibility Bar."

584
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:06,862
{\an8}BUSINESS CARD FROM ANOTHER BAR FOUND

585
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:08,572
{\an8}That's where Gun-mi used to work.

586
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:12,159
{\an8}He sure loves to drink for an attorney.

587
00:24:12,242 --> 00:24:13,493
{\an8}DOES THE PRIVILEGED RICH MAN
ENJOY THE NIGHTLIFE?

588
00:24:15,954 --> 00:24:16,955
{\an8}What's that?

589
00:24:17,038 --> 00:24:18,915
{\an8}CRUMPLED PAPER IN THE TRASH CAN

590
00:24:21,668 --> 00:24:24,004
{\an8}You've got to be kidding me.

591
00:24:24,087 --> 00:24:26,089
{\an8}She thinks a slap to her forehead
cured her text neck?

592
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:27,757
{\an8}"Do you believe there's a god,
Gold Spoon?"

593
00:24:27,841 --> 00:24:31,219
{\an8}"Well, I do.
Be my savior and my god, Gold Spoon."

594
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:33,930
It looks like Dancer has it bad again.

595
00:24:34,014 --> 00:24:35,348
FROM GOLD SPOON'S PRINCESS, AN DANCER

596
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:37,434
What the heck? What's this?

597
00:24:41,271 --> 00:24:43,190
{\an8}Why are all the nostrils heart-shaped?

598
00:24:44,274 --> 00:24:45,692
{\an8}What's this guy's deal?

599
00:24:46,193 --> 00:24:48,528
{\an8}Why does he keep photos like these?

600
00:24:52,741 --> 00:24:55,285
{\an8}A DOCUMENT ENVELOPE INSIDE THE DRAWER

601
00:24:56,453 --> 00:24:58,580
{\an8}A non-disclosure agreement
signed by Bang Libertine.

602
00:24:58,663 --> 00:25:00,749
{\an8}"Duty of confidentiality,

603
00:25:00,832 --> 00:25:01,958
{\an8}non-disclosure,

604
00:25:02,042 --> 00:25:04,044
{\an8}and compensation of five million won."

605
00:25:04,127 --> 00:25:05,170
{\an8}"Bang Libertine."

606
00:25:05,253 --> 00:25:06,213
{\an8}"Shin Fox."

607
00:25:07,047 --> 00:25:07,923
{\an8}"Park Hyeon-jun."

608
00:25:08,006 --> 00:25:08,840
{\an8}WHAT MUST BE KEPT SECRET?

609
00:25:09,841 --> 00:25:10,675
{\an8}Let's see.

610
00:25:11,176 --> 00:25:13,470
{\an8}HA GOLD SPOON'S PHONE

611
00:25:14,554 --> 00:25:15,597
{\an8}Let's check his messages.

612
00:25:16,473 --> 00:25:18,391
{\an8}"I'm Ha Gold Spoon,
the one you met at Sensibility."

613
00:25:18,475 --> 00:25:20,060
{\an8}"Then tell me which days you're free."

614
00:25:20,727 --> 00:25:21,937
{\an8}Is Gold Spoon serious?

615
00:25:27,275 --> 00:25:29,694
"Park Hyeon-jun, convenience store."

616
00:25:29,778 --> 00:25:31,613
Wait. What's this?

617
00:25:31,696 --> 00:25:32,697
{\an8}PARK HYEON-JUN/CONVENIENCE STORE

618
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:35,742
{\an8}I read these messages
on Lee Gun-mi's phone earlier.

619
00:25:36,535 --> 00:25:37,536
{\an8}What the heck?

620
00:25:38,787 --> 00:25:39,871
{\an8}"Memories of that day."

621
00:25:42,374 --> 00:25:43,917
They slept together.

622
00:25:46,086 --> 00:25:47,420
Mr. Attorney!

623
00:25:47,504 --> 00:25:49,714
Mr. Attorney,
I didn't expect this from you.

624
00:25:49,798 --> 00:25:51,508
I must admit, I'm a little disappointed.

625
00:25:56,012 --> 00:25:59,975
You must've been into clubbing.

626
00:26:05,021 --> 00:26:06,940
VIBING

627
00:26:07,023 --> 00:26:09,109
Hey, don't mess with that.

628
00:26:09,192 --> 00:26:11,278
That's reserved for the DJ!

629
00:26:11,361 --> 00:26:13,154
Come on, it's me you're talking to.

630
00:26:13,738 --> 00:26:15,282
{\an8}It's not like I haven't been here before.

631
00:26:15,365 --> 00:26:17,033
{\an8}HA GOLD SPOON IS NO STRANGER TO CLUBBING

632
00:26:17,117 --> 00:26:20,287
{\an8}I want to check out the club you work at.

633
00:26:20,370 --> 00:26:23,123
{\an8}I was rejected at the door
the last time I went there.

634
00:26:23,790 --> 00:26:25,709
{\an8}I think I know why. It's because...

635
00:26:25,792 --> 00:26:27,586
{\an8}- Never mind.
- Why? Tell me.

636
00:26:27,669 --> 00:26:28,712
{\an8}- Forget it.
- Tell me.

637
00:26:28,795 --> 00:26:31,089
{\an8}Come here. Just tell me, will you?

638
00:26:31,172 --> 00:26:32,048
{\an8}How could I?

639
00:26:32,132 --> 00:26:33,592
{\an8}CLUB SLAM

640
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:41,099
{\an8}Why's this door locked?

641
00:26:41,891 --> 00:26:43,226
{\an8}- What? It's over here.
- Hey, friend.

642
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:45,103
{\an8}The entrance is this way.

643
00:26:45,186 --> 00:26:46,271
{\an8}What?

644
00:26:46,354 --> 00:26:47,647
{\an8}What's this door, then?

645
00:26:47,731 --> 00:26:48,690
{\an8}What are you talking about?

646
00:26:49,566 --> 00:26:50,734
{\an8}Find your own way in.

647
00:26:50,817 --> 00:26:51,651
{\an8}A DOOR WITH A LOCK?

648
00:26:53,445 --> 00:26:55,989
{\an8}HEADING TO CLUB SLAM'S ACTUAL ENTRANCE

649
00:27:07,917 --> 00:27:10,420
I got bounced at the door once

650
00:27:10,503 --> 00:27:12,213
when I tried to get in.

651
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:14,883
I've made it my mission
to get inside a club at least once.

652
00:27:16,051 --> 00:27:19,471
{\an8}CONGRATULATIONS!
JANG C-STORE ENTERS A CLUB

653
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:25,143
I'd give anything to write my name
on a sign-in sheet.

654
00:27:25,769 --> 00:27:28,897
Why won't they let me into these places?

655
00:27:29,606 --> 00:27:31,316
August 8th.

656
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:35,111
Lee Gun-mi, a 27-year-old,
entered the club.

657
00:27:35,612 --> 00:27:38,031
Wasn't she friends with Dancer?

658
00:27:40,241 --> 00:27:41,785
An Dancer's break room.

659
00:27:43,411 --> 00:27:45,705
{\an8}SET UP IN THE CORNER OF THE CLUB

660
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:48,291
{\an8}A BREAK AREA FOR DANCERS

661
00:27:51,086 --> 00:27:53,129
{\an8}AN DANCER'S LOCKER

662
00:27:53,963 --> 00:27:55,590
I see she wanted to be a K-pop idol.

663
00:27:55,674 --> 00:27:57,258
ALWAYS DO A FIT CHECK!
YOU'LL BE AN IDOL ONE DAY

664
00:27:57,342 --> 00:27:58,677
{\an8}I'LL EVEN HAVE A MANAGER WHO FANS ME

665
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:00,512
{\an8}HOW DID AN ASPIRING IDOL
END UP AS A DANCER IN A CLUB?

666
00:28:02,222 --> 00:28:03,515
{\an8}An Dancer's phone is here.

667
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:07,977
{\an8}AN DANCER'S PHONE

668
00:28:09,437 --> 00:28:10,605
{\an8}AN DANCER'S CALL LOG

669
00:28:10,689 --> 00:28:12,899
{\an8}She talked to Kim Club for 22 seconds.

670
00:28:12,982 --> 00:28:15,819
She called Lee Gun-mi at 9:51 p.m.,

671
00:28:15,902 --> 00:28:17,445
talked to Kim Club at 10:05 p.m.,

672
00:28:18,154 --> 00:28:19,781
and called Lee Gun-mi again at 10:55 p.m.

673
00:28:20,782 --> 00:28:22,826
She talked to Lee Gun-mi at 9:20 p.m.

674
00:28:23,410 --> 00:28:25,203
and called her at 9:51 p.m. and 10:55 p.m.

675
00:28:25,286 --> 00:28:27,330
{\an8}She called,
but the calls didn't go through.

676
00:28:28,206 --> 00:28:30,625
{\an8}Lee Gun-mi, on the 12th.

677
00:28:32,377 --> 00:28:35,714
{\an8}"I'll be outside Slam
at 9:30 p.m. with the money."

678
00:28:35,797 --> 00:28:37,882
{\an8}"Gun-mi, we're still on for later, right?"

679
